{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "macros.html.j2" as m %}
{% block content %}
{% set latest = years[-1] %}
{% set p = pooled or latest %}
{% set h = highlights %}
{% macro pct(v, d=1) %}{{ ("%." ~ d ~ "f")|format(100 * v) }}%{% endmacro %}
{% macro lookup(phrase) %}<a href="?phrase={{ phrase | urlencode }}#explorer">{{ phrase }}</a>{% endmacro %}
{% macro rate_table(t, head, count_head="Talks / abstracts", val_head="Talk rate · 95% CI", link=False) %}
<div class="scroll"><table class="hl-table rates">
<thead><tr><th class="text">{{ head }}</th><th>{{ count_head }}</th><th class="text">{{ val_head }}</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for r in t.rows %}<tr><td class="text">{{ lookup(r.label) if link else r.label }}</td>
<td>{{ r.count }}</td>
<td class="text"><span class="rate"><span class="track">
<span class="ci" style="left:{{ '%.1f'|format(r.ci_left) }}%;width:{{ '%.1f'|format(r.ci_width) }}%"></span>
<span class="pt" style="left:{{ '%.1f'|format(r.bar) }}%"></span>
<span class="base" style="left:{{ '%.1f'|format(t.base) }}%"></span></span>
<span class="val">{{ r.val }}</span></span></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
{% endmacro %}
<h1>{{ page.title }}</h1>
<p class="lede">Every year the American Society of Human Genetics picks a few hundred of its several thousand accepted
abstracts for a talk; the rest become posters. This site parses the published abstracts
({{ years[0].year }}–{{ latest.year }}{% if pooled %}: {{ "{:,}".format(p.summary.abstracts) }} abstracts,
{{ "{:,}".format(p.summary.talks) }} talks{% endif %}) and asks which phrases, institutions and places show up more
often among talks.</p>
<p class="caveat"><strong>Read this first.</strong> Only <em>accepted</em> abstracts are published, so rejected
submissions never appear here, and authors can request a poster instead of a talk, so a poster does not mean an
abstract was passed over for a talk. “Talk rate” is the fraction of accepted abstracts presented as a talk, not an
acceptance rate or a quality score. Every number here is an association: it says how often a phrase, institution or
place goes with a talk, not that it earns one (adding a phrase to your abstract will not make it a talk), and
differences can reflect topic, field or what authors chose to submit. Not every affiliation could be matched to an
institution or place: see the <a href="methods.html#match-rates">match rates</a>.</p>

{% set ns = namespace(n=0) %}
{% if h %}
<section class="vignette" id="hot">
<h2>{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}<span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>What's hot at ASHG {{ h.latest }}</h2>
{% set r0 = h.rising[0] %}
<p class="lead">Topics that keep growing: “{{ r0.phrase }}” is in {{ pct(r0.last) }} of {{ h.latest }} abstracts, up
from {{ pct(r0.first) }} in {{ years[0].year }}.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table class="hl-table">
<thead><tr><th class="text">Topic</th><th>{{ years[0].year }}</th><th class="text spark-col">{{ years[0].year }}–{{ h.latest }}</th>
<th>{{ h.latest }}</th><th>Talks in {{ h.latest }}</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for r in h.rising %}<tr><td class="text">{{ lookup(r.phrase) }}</td><td>{{ pct(r.first) }}</td><td class="text spark-col">{{ r.spark }}</td>
<td><strong>{{ pct(r.last) }}</strong></td><td>{{ r.talks_last }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="table-note">Share of each year's accepted abstracts mentioning the topic (title or text; spelling variants count). Click a topic to look it up.
{% for r in h.rising if r.peak_year != h.latest %}“{{ r.phrase }}” peaked in {{ r.peak_year }} ({{ pct(r.peak) }}).{% endfor %}</p>
<p class="more-link"><a href="#explorer">Look up any phrase, year by year →</a></p>
<p class="more-link"><a href="phrases.html#phrase-trends">Phrase trends and biobanks →</a></p>
</section>

{% if drivers_json %}
<div class="vignette" id="search">
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{% call m.explorer(None, explorer_src, ns.n, "Search a phrase") %}
<p>Type a word or phrase to see how often talks and posters mention it each year, then which first-author institutions
and metro areas write about it. Hover or focus a row for that institution's own mention rate and odds of a talk.</p>
{% endcall %}
<p class="more-link"><a href="phrases.html#explorer">About the search, and phrase trends →</a></p>
</div>
{% endif %}

<section class="vignette" id="talk-leaning">
<h2>{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}<span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>What phrases are overrepresented in talks</h2>
<p class="lead">Among phrases in at least 10 talks, an abstract mentioning “{{ h.hot.rows[0].label }}” had
{{ h.hot.rows[0].val }} the odds of a talk of one that didn't.</p>
{{ rate_table(h.hot, "Phrase", count_head="Talks / posters", val_head="Odds of a talk · 95% CI", link=True) }}
<p class="table-note">The {{ h.hot.rows | length }} phrases with the strongest evidence of leaning toward talks (largest
z-score), sorted by odds of a talk with versus without the phrase; log scale, dashed line = 1× (as common in talks as
in posters). Click a phrase to look it up.</p>
{% if h.shift %}
<p><strong>Clinical work stopped leaning toward posters.</strong> Through {{ years[-2].year }},
{% for r in h.shift %}“{{ r.phrase }}”{{ ", " if loop.revindex > 2 else (" and " if not loop.last else "") }}{% endfor %} came up more often in posters than in talks; in {{ h.latest }} they were at least as common in talks.</p>
<div class="legend"><span><i style="background: var(--talk)"></i>share of talks</span><span><i style="background: var(--poster)"></i>share of posters</span></div>
<div class="scroll"><table class="hl-table">
<thead><tr><th class="text">Phrase</th><th class="text spark-col">{{ years[0].year }}–{{ h.latest }}</th>
<th>Odds of a talk {{ years[0].year }}–{{ years[-2].year % 100 }}</th><th>{{ h.latest }}</th><th>p (change)</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for r in h.shift %}<tr><td class="text">{{ lookup(r.phrase) }}</td><td class="text spark-col">{{ r.spark }}</td>
<td>{{ "%.2f"|format(r.or_before) }}×</td><td><strong>{{ "%.2f"|format(r.or_last) }}×</strong></td>
<td>{{ "< 0.001" if r.p < 0.001 else "%.3f"|format(r.p) }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="table-note">Each row on its own scale. These phrases were picked before looking at {{ h.latest }}, but across
every phrase tested no single shift survives a false-discovery-rate correction: <a href="phrases.html#shift">suggestive,
not established</a>.</p>
{% endif %}
<p class="more-link"><a href="phrases.html#by-year">Each year's top phrases →</a></p>
<p class="more-link"><a href="phrases.html#score">Score your own abstract →</a></p>
</section>

{% if h.words %}
{% set w0 = h.words.rows[0] %}
<section class="vignette" id="wording">
<h2>{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}<span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>{{ h.latest }} abstracts are worded differently</h2>
<p class="lead">“{{ w0.word }}” is in {{ pct(w0.share, 0) }} of {{ h.latest }} abstracts, up from
{{ pct(w0.share_before, 0) }} in {{ years[0].year }}–{{ years[-2].year }}. It is one of {{ h.words.n_sig }} words
significantly more common in {{ h.latest }}, and most of them are general wording rather than new topics.</p>
{% if "trends_words_enriched" in trends %}
{% if manhattan_src %}
<div class="mh" data-manhattan="enriched" data-src="{{ manhattan_src }}" data-label="Manhattan-style plot of every word, alphabetically, by minus log10 p for being more common in {{ h.latest }} abstracts than in earlier years, with a Bonferroni line.">
<img class="mh-fallback" src="img/trends_words_enriched.png" alt="Manhattan-style plot of every word, alphabetically, by minus log10 p for being more common in {{ h.latest }} abstracts than in earlier years, with a Bonferroni line; framework stands far above the rest." loading="lazy">
</div>
<p class="table-note">Every word, alphabetically, by how strongly it is overrepresented in {{ h.latest }}; dashed line: Bonferroni correction. Hover a point for its word, click it to look it up.</p>
{% else %}
{{ m.figure("img/trends_words_enriched.png", "Manhattan-style plot of every word, alphabetically, by minus log10 p for being more common in %s abstracts than in earlier years, with a Bonferroni line; framework stands far above the rest." % h.latest) }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

<div class="scroll"><table class="hl-table">
<thead><tr><th class="text">Word</th><th>{{ years[0].year }}–{{ years[-2].year }}</th><th>{{ h.latest }}</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for r in h.words.rows %}<tr><td class="text">{{ lookup(r.word) }}</td><td>{{ pct(r.share_before) }}</td><td><strong>{{ pct(r.share) }}</strong></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="table-note">Share of abstracts using each word (title or text). The most overrepresented words, one per family
of forms (“remain”, “remains”); one-sided Fisher's exact test per word, significant after Bonferroni correction over
{{ "{:,}".format(h.words.n) }} words. Click a word to see it in talks and posters, year by year.</p>
{% if words_enriched_json %}
{{ m.words_table(years, words_enriched_json, words_enriched_src, 10) }}
{% endif %}
<p class="more-link"><a href="phrases.html#words-enriched">Every word, interactive →</a></p>
<p class="more-link"><a href="#explorer">Look up any word in talks and posters, year by year →</a></p>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section class="vignette" id="institutions">
<h2>{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}<span class="num">{{ ns.n }}</span>Institutions with the highest talk rate</h2>
{% set i3 = h.inst.rows[:3] %}
<p class="lead">Among the {{ h.inst_pool }} institutions with the most first-author abstracts ({{ p.label }}),
{{ i3[0].label }}, {{ i3[1].label }} and {{ i3[2].label }} lead, at {{ pct(i3[2].talk_rate, 0) }}–{{ pct(i3[0].talk_rate, 0) }}
of abstracts given a talk, against {{ pct(h.baseline) }} overall.</p>
{{ rate_table(h.inst, "Institution") }}
<p class="table-note">First author's institutions; dashed line = all abstracts ({{ pct(h.baseline) }}). Smaller
institutions have wide intervals. In {{ h.latest }} alone, {{ h.latest_top | join(", ") }} had the highest rates.</p>
<p class="more-link"><a href="institutions.html">All 50 largest institutions, year by year →</a></p>
</section>

{% endif %}

{% endblock %}
